    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55360" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάσχετος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάτοχος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>held back, kept back</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατάσχετόν τι καλύπτειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					1253
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>held fast, possessed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κακίαις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Lib.</u>
					p.27
				</span></i>
			 O.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. δαιμονίῳ πνεύματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					1.31
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θείᾳ μέθῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.103
				</span></i>
			;  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς θεαῖς</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				Phalar.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				93.1
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἴστρῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.225
				</span></i>
			 (Paul. Sil.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύσσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Paus.
					8.19.3
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ Νυμφῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					10.12.11
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>inspired</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.4.7
			</span></i>.</div>
